WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.760
This story ended up being
more complicated than I thought.

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:06.360
It is generally accepted that
the oldest business in the world,

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.100
the oldest that’s
still operating, anyway,

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.740
is the Nishiyama Onsen Keiunkan.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:14.280
Which is this hot-springs hotel,
about three hours west of Tokyo.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:18.960
For one thousand three hundred years,
people have been coming here for

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.060
the natural, crystal-clear
hot water baths,

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:25.740
and until recently, the owners have
52 generations of the same family.

00:00:53.513 --> 00:00:55.380
There are other people staying
here tonight, by the way,

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:57.720
it’s just we’re not filming them
for obvious privacy reasons.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:58.680
The hotel's not empty.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.840
Anyway, I assumed that
I'd be staying in

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:02.400
something like a
living museum here,

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.380
because that's what
I've come to expect from

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:07.080
the sort of historical attractions
you'll find in Britain.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.400
That's what tends to happen

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.320
to anything centuries old
where I'm from:

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:14.400
a kind of preservation that means
that everything must be held

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.260
at a certain point in time,

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:20.040
funded by tourists who want to
visit the old thing and see history.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:22.080
Which is great if you're
running a museum,

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:25.380
but for a hotel business that needs
to survive in the 21st century:

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:27.780
well, customers will change
with the times.

00:02:26.901 --> 00:02:28.740
There’s still tradition here.
It's not a Western-style hotel.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:31.980
You sleep on futons, dinner is served
at a low Japanese-style table.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:35.580
But this place has been updated,
again and again and again,

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:37.560
this building is only
a few decades old,

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:39.540
the exact location has moved
around this area

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:40.680
many times over the years.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:44.040
It’s only been a hotel in the
English sense for a few decades,

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:47.700
before that it was just a place
to stay and take the waters.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.000
Now, there's very fast wifi and,
of course, a gift shop.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.460
They excavated new
hot springs in 2005,

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:55.620
which gave them five times
as much hot water,

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:59.100
and there are modern pumps and systems
to check water temperature and quality.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:00.840
The water's drinkable, by the way.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:02.820
It's a hot spring after all,
it’s mineral water.

00:03:34.438 --> 00:03:35.580
So that was going to be the story.

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:39.420
This is the world's oldest business,
because it changes with the times.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.700
Problem one with that:

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.340
the modern English-language
concept of "business"

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:46.380
doesn't quite map correctly onto

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:49.020
Japanese culture from more
than a millennium ago. Obviously.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:52.200
There is a school of flower arrangement
in Kyoto called Ikenobō,

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.120
that was founded a couple
of centuries before this.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:55.980
But that school
probably counts

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:58.380
as an "organisation" in English,
rather than “business”,

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:01.380
as best as I can tell from
translations and my local team here.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:03.120
If you do count that school,

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:07.200
you kind of have count much older
like the Catholic Church as well!

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.960
This has always been
a definite business.

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:11.700
So problem two:

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:14.940
this has only been the oldest business
in the world since 2006,

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:18.180
when the former record holder,
a construction company called Kongo Gumi,

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:19.140
fell on hard times.

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:21.960
But Kongo Gumi didn't close
or go bankrupt...

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.300
it was bought by a bigger
construction company.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:27.720
It had been a family business
for nearly 1500 years,

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.720
but now it's just a subsidiary
of a modern company,

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:34.260
still operating but arguably just
a name on an organisation chart.

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:38.640
Should Kongu Gumi still count?
I don't think so, but...

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:39.420
if it doesn't count,

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:41.700
that brings me to problem three
with this story,

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:44.940
which all the English-speaking sources
I found seem to have missed.

00:05:51.112 --> 00:05:53.880
There was no practical change
to what was happening here,

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:56.880
that seems more like a
restructure than a takeover?

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:59.400
The new owner is the
old general manager,

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:02.040
so while it’s not in the family,
there is continuity.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:04.740
And I hate to say "I'm not sure",

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:07.200
but if there's been one theme
through this channel

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.060
over the years I've
been making videos,

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:11.280
it's that the world
is complicated

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:13.980
and it doesn't fit in
neat little categories.

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:16.500
If you've got a list like
"oldest businesses"

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.660
that's a millennium
and a half old...

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:22.380
of course it's going to
have a few asterisks on it.

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:23.160
As for me...

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:26.220
I'm just going to go
and take the waters.

